1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:07,300
Dawn in Dessie did not just begin with mist and roasted coffee; it began with the village radio.

2
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:14,300
When my father Girma was eight, that grand wooden radio was the beating heart of our home.

3
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:21,800
One evening, the broadcast vanished. The radio fell silent; grandfather breathed a heavy sigh into the stillness.

4
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:29,300
Yet young Girma did not view silence as an ending, but as an invitation into a secret.

5
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:36,300
Amidst glowing glass bulbs and tangled copper coils, he found a single severed wire.

6
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:44,300
Without school, without a diploma; with pure patience and steady hands, he bonded the wires with heat.

7
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:51,800
With one turn of the dial… static burst into music, and Tilahun's beloved song filled the room!

8
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:59,800
Grandfather embraced Girma and said: 'He who mends what is broken with gentle hands learns how to listen to the world.'

9
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:07,300
Today, the neural pipelines we craft in code are no different from the copper wires my father soldered in Dessie.

10
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:14,800
The legacy of craft endures. Crafted with human vision and Artificial Intelligence.

